static TRAVEL_PLAN_SHORTLIST: &[(&[&str], &str)] = &[
    (&["honeymoon", "romantic", "anniversary", "just the two of us"], "Santorini and the Amalfi coast are the postcard picks, and both are heaving in July and August: Italy's lakes or Puglia give you the same views and food with fewer people. For a beach honeymoon with guaranteed sun, the Maldives from January to April, or Zanzibar if you want something less built up."),
    (&["toddler", "baby", "kids", "children", "child", "family", "teenager", "teenagers"], "With small children a short flight and a shallow beach beat a better destination: Menorca is the quietest of the Balearics, the Algarve has the sand and the short transfer, and a Center Parcs avoids the flight altogether. Book somewhere with a pool and a kitchen, and go in late May or September rather than the school summer, when it is warm but not 35C."),
    (&["weekend", "two nights", "long weekend", "few days"], "For a weekend the travel time is the whole trip, so pick somewhere under two hours door to door: Bath, York, the Cotswolds or the Norfolk coast at home, or Bruges, Lille or Amsterdam by train. Two nights is the right length, the train three or four weeks ahead is the cheap fare, and a room in the middle beats one with a car park."),
    (&["cheap", "budget", "afford", "money", "cost", "broke", "save", "pounds", "quid", "euros", "dollars", "spare"], "The cheapest sun is the Algarve or the Costa Blanca outside July and August: May, June and late September cost half the school-holiday price, and flights booked six to eight weeks ahead are the other half. Albania and Bulgaria's Black Sea coast are the best-value beaches in Europe, and Prague, Krakow and Budapest the cheap city breaks."),
    (&["quiet", "peaceful", "relaxing", "chill", "chilled", "calm", "restful", "escape it all", "away from crowds", "not too busy"], "Quiet comes from the place rather than the country: the north coast of Menorca and the Aran Islands are empty in June, the Alentejo and inland Andalucia have the heat without the resorts, and the Cotswolds, Northumberland or the far north of Scotland do it without a flight. Go in May, June or September - the same place in August is the crowd."),
    (&["beach", "beaches", "seaside", "coast", "sand", "sandy", "by the sea"], "Pick a stretch of coast rather than a town: the Norfolk coast, Pembrokeshire, Cornwall and the Northumberland coast are the easy ones at home, and the Algarve or the Costa Blanca give you warm water outside July and August. The beach a ten-minute walk from the car park is empty by ten, and the one with the car park and the cafe is not."),
    (&["city", "city break", "museums", "food", "restaurants", "culture", "shopping"], "Pick by what you want from a city: Lisbon for food and a short flight, Seville for heat and tapas, Prague or Budapest for grand streets at low prices, Copenhagen for design and cycling. Two nights is enough for any of them, and flying Tuesday to Thursday costs less than a weekend."),
    (&["ski", "snow", "skiing", "snowboard"], "A resort at 1,500m or above is what makes the snow reliable, and January and March are cheaper than February half-term for the same mountain. The French Alps have the highest villages, Austria the better-value lift passes, and Italy the cheapest of the big three. Book the transfer with the room, because a separate one is where the money goes."),
    (&["walking", "walk", "hike", "hiking", "mountains", "cycling", "outdoors"], "The Dolomites in late June or September for the big views and the huts, the Julian Alps for the same with fewer people, and the Lake District or the Peak District if you want a short break without a flight. Book the huts and the popular villages early, and carry the map on paper."),
    (&["sun", "sunny", "warm", "hot", "beach", "beaches", "swim", "swimming", "tan"], "For real sun at any time of year, the Canaries are the safe pick and the water is warmest from late summer into October. Greece in June or September gives you 28C without the August crowds, and from November to March the short-haul sun is the Canaries, Cape Verde or Egypt, with the Red Sea the one to swim in."),
    (&["uk", "britain", "england", "scotland", "wales", "staycation", "at home", "no flight"], "In the UK: Cornwall and the Pembrokeshire coast for beaches, the Lake District for walking, Northumberland for empty country and dark skies, and Edinburgh or Bath for a city. Book the coast two months ahead for a school holiday, and take the train where you can, because the drive is the part that eats the weekend."),
];
