const GIFT_CHEAP_ADULT: &str = "Spend it on something consumable and a notch better than the everyday: a good candle, decent coffee or tea, a nice bar of chocolate, a scratch card, seeds and a pot, a paperback you would actually recommend, or a really good pair of socks. £10 goes a long way on any of those and nothing needs a size or a taste test; if the group has a joke running, a silly gift that gets a laugh beats an expensive one that gets a polite smile. Keep the receipt.";
const GIFT_CHEAP_CHILD: &str = "For a child, spend it on things they use up or grow out of: bubble mix, a big sticker book, a colouring pad with good pens, bath crayons, play dough, a torch, a pack of cards, or a small Lego set on offer. Nothing needs a size and batteries are the only trap, so check the box. Socks, gloves and a book they will actually read are the safe last-minute ones.";
const GIFT_CHEAP_TEEN: &str = "For a teenager, a tenner is best spent on one thing they pick themselves: a voucher for the cinema or a shop they already use, phone credit, decent earphones or the cable they keep losing, or a game they can play with friends. Ask what they are into and buy the small version of that: the money goes further on one thing they want than on three they do not.";
const GIFT_TODDLER_GIFT: &str = "For a toddler, one thing they will use every day beats a pile of toys: a set of chunky blocks, a ball, a book with flaps to lift, or a scooter they will still fit next year. Ask the parents what they already have too much of, and buy the batteries with it.";
const GIFT_CHILD_GIFT: &str = "For that age, one thing they will use every day beats a pile of toys: a scooter, duplo, sticker and activity books, or a decent football. Ask the parents what they already have too much of, and buy the batteries with it. Wrap it in something they can play with afterwards.";
const GIFT_TEEN_GIFT: &str = "For a teenager, money or a voucher beats a guess, and headphones, gaming credit, a hoodie from a shop they like or a ticket to something are the safe few. Ask them once, buy the thing they named, and keep the change in a card with a real message in it.";
const GIFT_GROWN_GIFT: &str = "For that age, buy something they would use every week and would not buy themselves: good coffee or tea, a bottle of what they already drink, a voucher for a place they like, or a book by an author they follow. One useful thing beats a pile of small ones.";
const GIFT_GIFT_ANYONE: &str = "Buy into what they already do: a good version of something they use every week (a proper kitchen knife, warm socks, decent coffee), a voucher for a place they go anyway, or a day out the two of you share. Tell me what they do at the weekend and I'll narrow it down.";
