const COSTUME_METHOD: &str = "Ordinary clothes plus one big shape, and nothing to sew: a black hoodie with ears on a headband is a cat, a cardboard box is a robot, a dressing gown and a towel round the head is a shepherd. Hats, ears and face paint do more than the outfit, and one prop - a cardboard sword, a wooden spoon, a stack of books - tells everyone who it is meant to be.";
const TEA_FULL_KETTLE: &str = "A full 1.7-litre kettle makes about five or six mugs of tea, since a mug is around 300 ml and you lose a little to steam. A 1-litre kettle does three. Boil only what you are going to drink and it is quicker and cheaper both.";
const COMFORT_LAST: &str = "Say it plainly and don't rush to fix it: \"that's really hard, and I'm glad you told me.\" Ask what they need today - company, quiet, or a distraction - and offer one concrete thing, like a walk or dinner on Thursday, rather than \"let me know if you need anything\".";
