const TEXTURE_DOUGH: &[&str] = &["Add flour a spoonful at a time and knead it in before you judge, because a dough is wettest in the first few minutes: it should cling to your hand and come away clean. Wetter is better for an open crumb, so stop as soon as it stops running and keep a little of the water back next time, since flour alone can be 10% different in how much it drinks.", "Add water a spoonful at a time and knead a minute after each one: a stiff dough reads drier than it is, because the flour takes a few minutes to take up what is already in there, and you only feel the difference after kneading. A bread dough should be tacky rather than sticky - it clings to your hand but comes away clean - and it is ready when a piece stretches thin enough to see light through without tearing. If you overshoot, a spoonful of flour brings it back."];
